# The PROBING workload: positions whose search spends its time inside the Syzygy
# reader. One FEN per line; `#` and blank lines are stripped before the file reaches
# the engine.
#
# Why this file exists. Every position in the bench list has more men on it than any
# table `./build.sh tb-fetch` installs, so `registry.c`'s parse, `do_probe_table` and
# `decode_pairs` are ABSENT from every instruction figure this tree records. A bound
# placed inside the decode loop is free according to all of them, which is not the
# same as being free -- and the hardening in decode.c is exactly that kind of bound.
# `./build.sh perf-budget-tb` measures this instead, and the reader is ~31% of it.
#
# THE MATERIAL IS THE COVERED SET, NOT AN ARBITRARY ONE. `tb-fetch 5` installs
# KPvK/KNvK/KBvK/KRvK/KQvK and KNNvKP/KNNvK/KNvKP; every position below is one of
# those, so the root itself probes and the search stays inside the corpus as captures
# reduce it. A position outside the set only reaches the reader once it happens to
# reduce into it, which measures the search rather than the reader.
#
# THE CORPUS IS 5-MAN, so every figure taken over it is a LOWER BOUND. Block count
# scales with table size: the two walk loops in `decode_pairs` iterate less here than
# they would on a 6-man table, and the gate says so on every run.
#
# Golden: none. This is a workload, not an expected output -- `perf-budget-tb`
# compares an instruction count against a per-machine budget, and the node count it
# prints beside it is what tells a reader the workload itself did not move.

# KNNvKP, both colours, and with the pawn advanced: the largest tables in the set.
k7/p7/8/8/8/2N2N2/8/6K1 w - - 0 1
k7/p7/8/8/8/2N2N2/8/6K1 b - - 0 1
7k/7p/8/8/8/2N2N2/8/6K1 w - - 0 1

# KNvKP: one knight, so the search converges deeper into the reader per node.
k7/p7/8/8/8/5N2/8/6K1 w - - 0 1
7k/7p/8/8/8/5N2/8/6K1 b - - 0 1

# KNNvK: the child table the pawn capture reaches, probed on its own.
k7/8/8/8/8/2N2N2/8/6K1 w - - 0 1

# Two 3-man positions, which are the tables every other position reduces INTO.
8/8/8/3k4/8/8/5N2/4K3 w - - 0 1
8/8/8/3k4/8/8/5P2/4K3 w - - 0 1
